@startuml flow_s4_init_handshake
' Scenario 4 - Volt-Var HIL : startup handshake + teardown
' Verified against volt_var_controller.py (ArduinoSerialInterface.open /
' configure / close). Three-message handshake: INIT -> CFG -> P, each ACKed.
' Arduino capacitor reset happens at open(); END (at close) clears the
' firmware 'configured' flag before the port is closed.
'
' Render: plantuml -tsvg flow_s4_init_handshake.puml
'         plantuml -tpdf flow_s4_init_handshake.puml   (vector, for IEEE)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #1B1B1A
    LifeLineBorderColor #8A887F
    ParticipantBorderColor #1B1B1A
    ParticipantFontStyle bold
}

participant "RPi host\n(configure())" as RPi
participant "Arduino firmware\n(Uno R3, 115200)" as FW

== Open (open()) ==
RPi -> FW : serial open on /dev/ttyACM0
note over FW : capacitor reset\n(ARDUINO_RESET_DELAY_S wait)\ninput buffer flushed

== Handshake (configure()) ==
RPi -> FW : INIT:<n>
FW --> RPi : ACK:INIT

RPi -> FW : CFG:q_ratio,u1,u2,u3,u4
FW --> RPi : ACK:CFG
note right of FW : stores Q(V) curve\nP: rejected as ERR:CFG_BEFORE_P\nuntil CFG received

RPi -> FW : P:<p1,p2,...>
FW --> RPi : ACK:P
note right of FW : stores installed P[]\nconfigured = true

== Per-timestep loop (Diagram 2) ==
loop each timestep
    RPi -> FW : V:<vm>   (4-decimal ASCII)
    FW --> RPi : Q:<q>
end

== Teardown (close()) ==
RPi -> FW : END
note over FW : firmware clears configured
RPi -> RPi : port closed

@enduml
